Milestone 3 : Automation using Flow Designer & Email Notification.

When a student creates a new IT support ticket, they only need to enter the Caller Name and Short Description of the issue. The student does not need to manually select the Category or Subcategory. Once the ticket is submitted, a Flow Designer automation is triggered and evaluates the Short Description for predefined keywords such as WiFi, Projector, Password, or Slow. Based on the identified keyword, the flow automatically assigns the appropriate Category and Subcategory to the ticket. 
•	If the short description contains the word WiFi, the flow assigns Category = Network and Subcategory = WiFi.
•	If the description contains Projector, the flow assigns Category = Hardware and Subcategory = Projector.
•	If the description includes Password or Login, the flow assigns Category = Access and Subcategory = Forgot Password.
•	If the description mentions Slow or Hanging, the flow assigns Category = Performance and Subcategory = Slow Computer.

This automation ensures consistent classification, eliminates human error, and significantly reduces the manual effort required by IT staff. 
The entire process is implemented using Flow Designer, making the solution easy to maintain, scalable, and completely no-code.

